# Project: Form Component Development Standards

## Form Component Overview

Form components in Typerefinery follow a standardized architecture pattern that ensures consistency, maintainability, and integration with the form system, Flow API, and client-side data collection.

**Base Component**: `typerefinery/components/forms/field`  
**Location**: `/apps/typerefinery/components/forms/fields/`  
**Reference**: See `docs/forms/developer-guide.md` for comprehensive development guide

## Core Architecture Principles

### 1. Inheritance via Resource Super Type

**MANDATORY**: All form field components MUST extend `typerefinery/components/forms/field` via `sling:resourceSuperType`.

```json
{
  "isContainer": false,
  "group": "Typerefinery - Forms",
  "sling:resourceType": "ws:Component",
  "sling:resourceSuperType": "typerefinery/components/forms/field",
  "description": "Component description",
  "title": "Component Title"
}
```

**Rules:**
- **REQUIRED**: `sling:resourceSuperType` must be `"typerefinery/components/forms/field"`
- **REQUIRED**: `group` must be `"Typerefinery - Forms"` to appear in form component palette
- **REQUIRED**: `isContainer` should be `false` unless component needs to contain children
- Component definitions go in `/apps/typerefinery/components/forms/fields/{component}/.content.json`

### 2. Sling Model Pattern

**MANDATORY**: All form field components MUST have a Sling Model that extends `BaseFormComponent`.

```java
@Model(adaptables = {
    Resource.class,
    SlingHttpServletRequest.class
}, defaultInjectionStrategy = OPTIONAL)
@Exporter(name = "jackson", extensions = "json", options = {
    @ExporterOption(name = "SerializationFeature.WRITE_DATES_AS_TIMESTAMPS", value = "true")
})
public class YourComponent extends BaseFormComponent {
    
    protected static final String DEFAULT_MODULE = "yourcomponent";
    protected static final String DEFAULT_LABEL = "Your Label";
    protected static final String DEFAULT_PLACEHOLDER = "Your placeholder";
    
    @Inject
    @Getter
    @Default(values = "defaultValue")
    public String yourProperty;
    
    @Override
    @PostConstruct
    protected void init() {
        this.module = DEFAULT_MODULE;
        super.init();
        
        if (StringUtils.isBlank(label)) {
            this.label = DEFAULT_LABEL;
        }
        
        if (StringUtils.isBlank(placeholder)) {
            this.placeholder = DEFAULT_PLACEHOLDER;
        }
        
        style.addClasses("form-control");
    }
}
```

**Rules:**
- **REQUIRED**: Extend `ai.typerefinery.websight.models.components.forms.BaseFormComponent`
- **REQUIRED**: Use `@Model` with `Resource.class` and `SlingHttpServletRequest.class` as adaptables
- **REQUIRED**: Use `@Exporter` with `"jackson"` name and `"json"` extension
- **REQUIRED**: Override `init()` method, call `super.init()` first
- **REQUIRED**: Set `this.module` to component-specific module name
- **REQUIRED**: Use `@Inject`, `@Getter` (Lombok), and `@Default` for properties
- Package: `ai.typerefinery.websight.models.components.forms`

### 3. Template Structure

**MANDATORY**: Form field components MUST follow the standard template structure.

#### Main Template (`{component}.html`)

```html
<!--/* Copyright header */-->
<sly data-sly-use.model="ai.typerefinery.websight.models.components.forms.YourComponent">
  <div class="${model.componentClassNames}"> 
    <sly data-sly-use.template="./variant.html" data-sly-call="${template.variant @ model=model}">
    </sly>
  </div>
</sly>
```

**Rules:**
- **REQUIRED**: Adapt the component-specific Sling Model
- **REQUIRED**: Use `model.componentClassNames` for CSS classes
- **REQUIRED**: Include `variant.html` template via `data-sly-call`
- The base `field/variant.html` handles label wrapper - your variant provides the input element

#### Variant Template (`variant.html`)

```html
<template data-sly-template.variant="${ @ model }">
  <input 
    component="${model.componentName}"
    id="${model.id}" 
    name="${model.name}"
    value="${model.value}"
    data-fieldId="${model.parentFieldId}" 
    placeholder="${model.placeholder}" 
    class="${model.variantClassNames}"
    data-model="${model.jsonString}"
  />
</template>
```

**Rules:**
- **REQUIRED**: Use `data-sly-template.variant` pattern
- **REQUIRED**: Include `component`, `id`, `name`, `data-fieldId`, `data-model` attributes
- **REQUIRED**: Use model properties for attribute values
- **REQUIRED**: Include `data-model` with `model.jsonString` for client-side data access
- The base field component's variant handles label wrapper automatically

### 4. Dialog Configuration

**MANDATORY**: Dialog configurations MUST use shared fragments from `forms/form/common/`.

```json
{
  "sling:resourceType": "wcm/dialogs/dialog",
  "tabs": {
    "sling:resourceType": "wcm/dialogs/components/tabs",
    "generalTab": {
      "sling:resourceType": "wcm/dialogs/components/tab",
      "label": "General",
      "fieldName": {
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/dialogs/components/include",
        "path": "/apps/typerefinery/components/forms/form/common/fieldName"
      },
      "placeholder": {
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/dialogs/components/include",
        "path": "/apps/typerefinery/components/forms/form/common/placeholder"
      },
      "fieldValue": {
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/dialogs/components/include",
        "path": "/apps/typerefinery/components/forms/form/common/fieldValue"
      }
    },
    "eventTab": {
      "sling:resourceType": "wcm/dialogs/components/tab",
      "label": "Events",
      "event": {
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/dialogs/components/multifield",
        "name": "_events_",
        "label": "Events",
        "topic": {
          "sling:resourceType": "wcm/dialogs/components/include",
          "path": "/apps/typerefinery/components/dialog/tabs/event/event/topic"
        },
        "type": {
          "sling:resourceType": "wcm/dialogs/components/include",
          "path": "/apps/typerefinery/components/dialog/tabs/event/event/type"
        },
        "eventAction": {
          "sling:resourceType": "typerefinery/components/dialog/eventactions",
          "name": "action",
          "label": "Component Action"
        }
      }
    },
    "validationTab": {
      "sling:resourceType": "wcm/dialogs/components/include",
      "path": "/apps/typerefinery/components/dialog/tabs/validation"
    },
    "gridTab": {
      "sling:resourceType": "wcm/dialogs/components/include",
      "path": "/apps/typerefinery/components/dialog/tabs/grid"
    },
    "styleTab": {
      "sling:resourceType": "wcm/dialogs/components/include",
      "path": "/apps/typerefinery/components/dialog/tabs/style"
    },
    "ariaTab": {
      "sling:resourceType": "wcm/dialogs/components/include",
      "path": "/apps/typerefinery/components/dialog/tabs/aria"
    }
  }
}
```

**Rules:**
- **REQUIRED**: Use shared fragments from `/apps/typerefinery/components/forms/form/common/`
- **REQUIRED**: Include standard tabs: General, Events, Validation, Grid, Style, Aria
- **REQUIRED**: Include common fields: `fieldName`, `placeholder`, `fieldValue` (and others as needed)
- **REQUIRED**: Use includes for shared dialog components to ensure consistency
- Add component-specific fields in `generalTab` as needed

### 5. Client Libraries (Optional)

**OPTIONAL**: Client libraries are only needed if component requires JavaScript or CSS.

#### Structure

```
/clientlibs/
├── .content.json
├── behaviour.js
├── functions.js
└── style.css
```

#### `.content.json`

```json
{
  "sling:resourceType": "io/typerefinery/websight/clientlibs",
  "categories": ["ai.typerefinery.websight.components"],
  "css": [
    "/apps/typerefinery/components/forms/fields/{component}/clientlibs/style.css"
  ],
  "js": [
    "/apps/typerefinery/components/forms/fields/{component}/clientlibs/behaviour.js",
    "/apps/typerefinery/components/forms/fields/{component}/clientlibs/functions.js"
  ]
}
```

**Rules:**
- **OPTIONAL**: Only include if component needs JavaScript or CSS
- **REQUIRED**: Use category `"ai.typerefinery.websight.components"` for auto-discovery
- **REQUIRED**: Use absolute paths starting with `/apps/`
- **REQUIRED**: `behaviour.js` should call `watchDOMForComponent` for DOM initialization
- Component clientlibs are automatically included when page includes component category

## Component Structure

### Required Files

```
/apps/typerefinery/components/forms/fields/{component}/
├── .content.json              # Component definition (REQUIRED)
├── {component}.html           # Main template (REQUIRED)
├── variant.html               # Field variant template (REQUIRED)
└── dialog/
    └── .content.json          # Dialog configuration (REQUIRED)
```

### Optional Files

```
/apps/typerefinery/components/forms/fields/{component}/
├── clientlibs/                # Optional: JavaScript/CSS
│   ├── .content.json
│   ├── behaviour.js
│   ├── functions.js
│   └── style.css
├── eventactions/              # Optional: Event action definitions
│   └── .content.json
└── README.md                  # REQUIRED: Component documentation
```

**MANDATORY**: All form components MUST have a `README.md` file.

### Java Sling Model

```
/application/backend/src/main/java/ai/typerefinery/websight/models/components/forms/
└── {YourComponent}.java       # Sling Model class (REQUIRED)
```

## Integration Points

### 1. Form Data Collection

**AUTOMATIC**: All form field components are automatically collected by the form's `getFormData()` function.

**Rules:**
- Component must have `name` attribute on input element
- Component must include `data-model` attribute with `model.jsonString`
- Field values are collected based on `name` attribute
- Array values (checkboxes, multi-select) are handled automatically

### 2. Flow API Integration

**AUTOMATIC**: Field components are automatically included in Flow payloads when form has Flow enabled.

**Rules:**
- No special configuration needed for basic fields
- Flow metadata (enablement, templates) is configured on parent form
- Field values are included in Flow payload automatically
- Composite fields can output as objects or arrays based on variant

### 3. Event System

**OPTIONAL**: Components can emit and listen to events via `Typerefinery.Page.Events`.

**Rules:**
- Use `eventactions/.content.json` to define component-specific actions
- Wire events in dialog's `eventTab`
- Events are handled by form client library (`functions.js`)
- Standard events: `FORM_SUCCESS`, `FORM_ERROR`, `FORM_SUBMIT`, `FORM_CANCEL`, `FORM_LOAD`

## BaseFormComponent Properties

All form components inherit these properties from `BaseFormComponent`:

- `id` - Unique field ID
- `name` - Field name (used in form submission)
- `label` - Field label
- `value` - Field value
- `placeholder` - Placeholder text
- `disabled` - Disabled state
- `required` - Required validation
- `module` - Client module name
- `componentClassNames` - CSS classes for component wrapper
- `variantClassNames` - CSS classes for field element
- `jsonString` - JSON representation of model (for `data-model` attribute)

